.el .ds Aq '
.TH lrsalvage 1  "lrsalvage 0.4.0" 
.SH NAME
lrsalvage \- Recover JPEG previews from Adobe Lightroom Classic catalogs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlrsalvage\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a Lightroom catalog and its preview cache, and writes out the largest cached JPEG for every image whose original file is gone.
.PP
Everything is opened read\-only. Output never lands inside the catalog or the preview cache.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBscan\fR
Report what is recoverable. Writes nothing except the files you name
.TP
\fBextract\fR
Write the recoverable JPEGs, plus a report and a JSON manifest
.TP
\fBmasks\fR
Decode `.lrcat\-data` AI mask layers to PNG
.SH SCAN
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBlrsalvage scan\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-contact\-sheet\fR] [\fB\-\-report\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-long\-edge\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-long\-edge\fR] [\fB\-\-all\-levels\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-present\fR] [\fB\-\-verify\-source\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-catalog\fR> <\fB\-\-previews\fR> 
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-catalog\fR \fI<CATALOG>\fR
Catalog file (`*.lrcat`)
.TP
\fB\-\-previews\fR \fI<PREVIEWS>\fR
Preview cache directory (`* Previews.lrdata`)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a machine\-readable summary instead of a table
.TP
\fB\-\-contact\-sheet\fR \fI<CONTACT_SHEET>\fR
Write a self\-contained HTML contact sheet of the best previews
.TP
\fB\-\-report\fR \fI<REPORT>\fR
Write the path\-free verification report to this file
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print one line per plan item instead of only totals
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-long\-edge\fR \fI<MIN_LONG_EDGE>\fR [default: 640]
Ignore previews below this long edge
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-long\-edge\fR \fI<MAX_LONG_EDGE>\fR [default: 0]
Write the largest preview at or below this long edge, not the largest present. `0` disables the cap
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-levels\fR
Inspect every level, not only the best one
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-present\fR
Also include images whose original file is still present
.TP
\fB\-\-verify\-source\fR
Prove the catalog was only read: hash it, copy it, hash the copy, and fail if the two disagree.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRACT
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBlrsalvage extract\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-long\-edge\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-long\-edge\fR] [\fB\-\-all\-levels\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-present\fR] [\fB\-\-verify\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-metadata\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-timestamps\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-catalog\fR> <\fB\-\-previews\fR> <\fB\-\-out\fR> 
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-catalog\fR \fI<CATALOG>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-previews\fR \fI<PREVIEWS>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Destination directory. Must not be inside the catalog or cache
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Do everything except write files
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-long\-edge\fR \fI<MIN_LONG_EDGE>\fR [default: 640]
Ignore previews below this long edge
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-long\-edge\fR \fI<MAX_LONG_EDGE>\fR [default: 0]
Write the largest preview at or below this long edge, not the largest present. `0` disables the cap
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-levels\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-include\-present\fR
Also include images whose original file is still present
.TP
\fB\-\-verify\-source\fR
Prove the catalog was only read: hash it, copy it, hash the copy, and fail if the two disagree.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-metadata\fR
Do not add EXIF, XMP rating or the ICC profile to the recovered JPEGs.

Such output carries no marker, so a later run cannot prove it wrote the file: every destination is reported as not a verified extraction and is left untouched unless \-\-force is given.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-timestamps\fR
Do not set file modification times to the capture time
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing destination file that is not a verified extraction
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH MASKS
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBlrsalvage masks\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-data\fR> <\fB\-\-out\fR> 
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<DATA>\fR
A `<catalog>.lrcat\-data` directory
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success, including \-\-help and \-\-version.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Usage or input error: bad arguments, a catalog that cannot be read, or a preview cache path that is not a directory.
.TP
\fB2\fR
extract completed, and at least one selected image could not be written.
.TP
\fB3\fR
Nothing was selected to do.
.TP
\fB4\fR
Unsafe, unwritable or too small a destination: the destination is inside the evidence, cannot be written, or does not have the free space this run would still write.
.TP
\fB5\fR
The catalog changed while it was being read, so nothing was planned from the copy.
.SH VERSION
v0.4.0
